Don't redefine FILE_ID_INFO on mingw-w64 toolchains that provide it

Qt 5.7 defines FILE_ID_INFO itself whenever it is compiled by mingw, on the
assumption that the toolchain headers do not have it. It guards the
neighbouring FILE_ID_128 fallback with FILE_SUPPORTS_INTEGRITY_STREAMS but
applies no such guard here.

mingw-w64 declares FILE_ID_INFO in winbase.h under

    #if _WIN32_WINNT >= _WIN32_WINNT_WIN8

and recent versions default _WIN32_WINNT to Windows 8 or later when the build
does not set it, so both definitions are visible and the compile fails with

    error: redefinition of 'struct _FILE_ID_INFO'
    error: conflicting declaration 'typedef int FILE_ID_INFO'

Guard Qt's definition with the same condition the toolchain uses, so it is only
declared when the headers do not already provide it. On older mingw-w64, where
_WIN32_WINNT defaults lower and winbase.h omits the struct, Qt's definition is
still used and behaviour is unchanged.

--- old/qtbase/src/corelib/io/qfilesystemengine_win.cpp
+++ new/qtbase/src/corelib/io/qfilesystemengine_win.cpp
@@ -631,10 +631,12 @@
 } FILE_ID_128, *PFILE_ID_128;
 #    endif // !(Q_CC_MINGW && FILE_SUPPORTS_INTEGRITY_STREAMS)

+#    if !(defined(Q_CC_MINGW) && defined(_WIN32_WINNT) && _WIN32_WINNT >= 0x0602)
 typedef struct _FILE_ID_INFO {
     ULONGLONG VolumeSerialNumber;
     FILE_ID_128 FileId;
 } FILE_ID_INFO, *PFILE_ID_INFO;
+#    endif // !(Q_CC_MINGW && _WIN32_WINNT >= _WIN32_WINNT_WIN8)
 #  endif // if defined (Q_CC_MINGW) || (defined(Q_CC_MSVC) && (_MSC_VER < 1700 || WINVER <= 0x0601))

 // File ID for Windows up to version 7.
